/T (In this code we are exposed the application from anywhere \(inside & outside\) We need to Give public ip of node where pod is running. Node Port Range= 30000 - 32767 here i hae defined port number as 30001 if we dont specify the port it will assign automatically. kubectl apply -f filename.yml. NodePort expose service on a static port on each node. NodePort services are typically used for smaller applications with a lower traffic volume. To avoid this we are using the LoadBalancer service. Just Replace NodePort=LoadBalancer)
/E (In this code we are exposed the application from anywhere \(inside & outside\) We need to Give public ip of node where pod is running. Node Port Range= 30000 - 32767 here i hae defined port number as 30001 if we dont specify the port it will assign automatically. kubectl apply -f filename.yml. NodePort expose service on a static port on each node. NodePort services are typically used for smaller applications with a lower traffic volume. To avoid this we are using the LoadBalancer service. Just Replace NodePort=LoadBalancer)
/Pg 54 0 R
/K [0]
>>
